act evidence: TASK-260720-1zntv0_review-verdict.md.\\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260721-d3b8bc, pid=97569, exit=0)\\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260721-d0a95b, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (codex) (run=RUN-260721-d0a95b)\\nRework logbook 2026-07-21 — stop-the-line architecture conflict confirmed against Go 1.25 and native macOS APIs. The supported-platform AC requires per-child filesystem and network denial plus resource and process-graph controls on Ubuntu, macOS, and Windows, while the normative graph permits only direct Go and GOROOT tool executables. Darwin os/exec has no per-child sandbox hook; sandbox_init confines the current process and sandbox-exec is an extra deprecated launcher. Linux requires child pre-exec namespace, Landlock/seccomp/cgroup setup or a broker; Windows needs a custom suspended-process, Job Object, restricted-token/AppContainer subsystem. Post-start observation is racy and permission/environment checks do not enforce denial. Failing closed outside one host contradicts valid real-build support on current CI. No product code changed. Recommended decision: permit one operator-trusted manager-owned sandbox launcher or broker and revise conformance, or explicitly narrow supported build hosts. Full evidence and tradeoffs: TASK-260720-1zntv0_host-policy-blocker.md.\\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260721-d0a95b, pid=2376, exit=0)\\nRevalidation 2026-07-27: curator-spec origin/main remains 57c1f56846d221ecc55786bd3c2467ec32f11730 with no rc.4 tag/ref; Curator origin/main remains 17804ceae42d3bb62abf6e8a9d9cbef6dd5370b8; cocoaskills origin/main remains 6fc2fd97dbdf40f5b0e46f846eaa0d78a1b33d12. The accepted design still normatively requires direct launch of fingerprinted go while also requiring readonly source/toolchain presentation, network denial, resource limits, and process-graph enforcement. No existing text admits a manager re-exec, launcher, or broker. TASK-260720-1zntv0 therefore remains blocked on the documented human architecture decision: permit one fixed operator-trusted manager-owned sandbox launcher/broker and revise protocol/conformance, or narrow supported go-v1 hosts and fail closed elsewhere. No product code or release provenance changed.\\nArchitecture analysis directive 2026-07-27: produce an implementation-ready decision packet that compares only the two viable contracts already documented. Analyze whether a fixed manager-owned re-exec of the exact Curator executable can serve as the trusted sandbox boundary without any third-party/package-controlled executable; define TCB and fingerprint/identity requirements, exact process graph, package influence exclusions, and Linux/macOS/Windows enforcement primitives for filesystem read/write/execute, network, process tree, memory/process/disk/time/output controls. Identify any platform profile where enforcement still cannot be fail-closed. Map every required amendment to curator-spec protocol/profile/security/schema/vector/driver/cache semantics and every Curator/csk implementation/test/CI consequence. State whether go-v1 may retain its identifier before rc.4 or requires a new driver/policy identifier. Compare against narrowing supported hosts. Recommend one option with explicit residual risks and the exact human decision sentence. Research/analysis only: do not modify product code, candidate spec files, release metadata, refs, pins, or provenance. Persist the packet as a task outcome resource and leave the task blocked if human authorization remains necessary.\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (codex) (run=RUN-260727-791dca, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (codex) (run=RUN-260727-791dca)\\n2026-07-27 solution-architecture finding: the direct Go os/exec graph cannot install the required native filesystem/network/process/resource controls before compiler execution. Of the two documented contracts, recommend one identity-verified manager-owned worker plus a fail-closed capability-gated hardened Linux profile; current macOS and Windows profiles must reject before worker/Go. Retain go-v1 before unreleased rc.4 only with an explicit manager-worker-v1 cache/receipt policy revision. Justified gap self-check covered protocol/core §4.2, profiles/manager §§2.2–2.4, SECURITY compile-only/compiler-input, decision 0004, closed policy schema, accepted contract research, and rejected/out-of-scope alternatives: the fixed worker is not package-selected, but the graph change requires human authorization. No new board tasks were created because existing spec, Curator, csk, and downstream owners are the smallest traceable decomposition and implementation must not be presumed before authorization. Exact decision and task/CI map are attached in TASK-260720-1zntv0_host-execution-decision.md.\\nagent completed: [analyst] solution-architect (codex) (exit=0)\\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260727-791dca, pid=42911, exit=0)\\nIndependent review directive 2026-07-27: review only the new host-execution decision packet and its board/resource integrity. Verify claims against authoritative platform documentation and the current accepted candidate contract; challenge the conclusion that hardened Linux is the only positive profile and that macOS/Windows must fail closed. Check worker identity/TOCTOU, authenticated list-to-build state machine, source mutation boundary, package influence exclusions, exact process graph, resource/disk/descendant controls, csk Python TCB implications, driver identifier versus policy revision, cache/receip