{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"agent_message","text":"Verdict: stop-the-line confirmed. `TASK-260720-1zntv0 — Implement go-v1 preflight and artifact build` is now `blocked`; the implementation is not accepted.\n\nThe decision packet is sound:\n\n- Hardened Linux is viable only with fail-closed capability probes using Landlock, namespaces, cgroup memory/process controls, tree kill, and bounded tmpfs. [Landlock](https://cdn.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/userspace-api/landlock.html), [cgroup v2](https://docs.kernel.org/admin-guide/cgroup-v2.html)\n- macOS lacks the required external-executable and aggregate resource contract. [App Sandbox file access](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/security/accessing-files-from-the-macos-app-sandbox), [`setrlimit`](https://developer.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/System/Conceptual/ManPages_iPhoneOS/man2/setrlimit.2.html)\n- Windows has useful Job Object/AppContainer controls, but the fuller sandbox API remains experimental. [Job Objects](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/procthread/job-objects), [experimental sandbox API](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/secauthz/createprocessinsandbox)\n\nThe persisted evidence is [TASK-260720-1zntv0_host-execution-review.md](/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/curator/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1zntv0/TASK-260720-1zntv0_host-execution-review.md).\n\nExact decision required:\n\n> Authorize protocol 1.0.0-rc.4 to permit one identity-verified manager-owned sandbox worker in the fixed go-v1 process graph, retain the `go-v1` identifier with a new `manager-worker-v1` execution-policy cache revision, and ship real builds only on the fail-closed hardened Linux profile; macOS and Windows must reject go-v1 until independently reviewed native profiles satisfy the same executable, filesystem, network, and resource gates.\n\nNo product, candidate, release, pin, ref, or provenance files changed. Global board validation still reports 45 unrelated pre-existing issues."}}
